<Project>

  <!--
    This file exists to override one Windows App SDK target, and is imported after the SDK's own
    .targets, which is what lets the override win.

    Keep the parent chain alive: MSBuild stops at the first Directory.Build.targets it finds walking
    up from the project, so without this import a future one at the repository root would be ignored.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_ParentDirectoryBuildTargets>$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.targets', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))</_ParentDirectoryBuildTargets>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <Import Project="$(_ParentDirectoryBuildTargets)" Condition="'$(_ParentDirectoryBuildTargets)' != ''" />

  <!--
    The Windows App SDK adds GetVCInstallPath to the XAML compiler's DependsOn lists for every
    project, C++ or not. That target runs a GetLatestMSVCVersion task which enumerates
    "$(VsInstallRoot)\VC\Tools\MSVC" and throws DirectoryNotFoundException when the MSVC toolset is
    not installed. VsInstallRoot is only set when building inside Visual Studio, which is why command
    line builds succeed while Visual Studio builds fail with:

        The "GetLatestMSVCVersion" task failed unexpectedly.
        System.IO.DirectoryNotFoundException: Could not find a part of the path
        '...\VC\Tools\MSVC'.

    BackupAssistant is a C#-only app and has no use for the MSVC toolset. The paths that target
    computes are only ever passed to the XAML compiler for reading C++ metadata, and the sibling
    GetXamlCppIncludeDirectories target is already correctly skipped for managed projects. Replacing
    it with an empty target leaves VCInstallPath32/64 unset - exactly the state of a working command
    line build - and spares every developer a multi-gigabyte C++ workload install.

    Note this is a full replacement, not a conditional fallback: when two targets share a name the
    last definition wins outright. Only do this in a folder that holds no C++ projects.

    Remove once the Windows App SDK guards GetVCInstallPath on '$(ManagedAssembly)'.
  -->
  <Target Name="GetVCInstallPath" />

</Project>
